---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { pages } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout page={pages["about"]}>
  <section class="section intro">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">HELLO. WE’RE CARDISTRY.</p>
      <h2>
        Built around
        <br />
        <em>the human moment.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="lead">
        The handshake. The good conversation. The “let’s work together”. That’s what a
        business card is really for.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cardistry brings thoughtful print and direct-data technology together to make that
        moment easier. A card should look like your brand, feel considered and do its job
        without unnecessary complications.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our approach is straightforward: custom PVC cards, NFC when you want it, and an
        optional contact QR. No mandatory hosted profile. No monthly subscription for
        direct-data sharing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="statement">
    <p class="eyebrow">OUR PHILOSOPHY</p>
    <h2>
      Keep the card.
      <br />
      <em>Lose the complications.</em>
    </h2>
  </section>
  <section class="section three-grid">
    <article>
      <h3>Design with intention.</h3>
      <p>
        A clear hierarchy and a distinct identity make a small card work harder. We leave
        room for the information that matters.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Technology with a purpose.</h3>
      <p>
        Direct-data sharing is a deliberate choice, not a universal compatibility claim.
        We explain both the benefits and the limits.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A more reusable introduction.</h3>
      <p>
        An NFC card can be kept and used for repeated introductions, reducing the need to
        hand out a new paper card each time.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
